analysisWe need to output an assert statement corresponding to comment:

// @@@ If the role is not null, then the role is contained in the list after adding it.

Method add(Role role) throws IllegalArgumentException, and inside it checks if role == null throw IllegalArgumentException. So precondition: role != null (otherwise exception). The comment says: If the role is not null, then the role is contained in the list after adding it.

Thus assert: role != null => this.contains(role). But after addition, role is definitely not null (since we only get here if not null). So we can assert this.contains(role). However spec says "If the role is not null, then the role is contained in the list after adding it." So we need to express implication: role != null => this.contains(role). Since method throws exception for null, we could also just assert this.contains(role) assuming role not null. But follow pattern: use implication.

Thus final assert: assert role != null => this.contains(role);

